# Marks and the jump list (marks.ts).

=== 'a goes to the mark's line, `a to the mark
text:
one
tw|o
three
keys: maG'a
want:
one
|two
three

=== `a goes to the mark itself
text:
one
tw|o
three
keys: maG`a
want:
one
tw|o
three

=== a mark follows edits above it
text:
one
tw|o
keys: makOnew<Esc>j0`a
want:
new
one
tw|o

=== a mark whose text went is not set
text:
one
tw|o
three
keys: maggjdd`a
want:
one
|three
error: yes

=== d'a deletes lines to the mark
text:
|one
two
three
four
keys: jjmaggd'a
want:
|four

=== y`a yanks to the mark (exclusive)
text:
|hello world
keys: wmaggy`aP
want:
hello| hello world

=== '' goes back where the last jump began
text:
|one
two
three
keys: jG''
want:
one
|two
three

=== `` swaps back and forth
text:
o|ne
two
three
keys: G````
want:
one
two
|three

=== an unset mark is an error
text:
|one
keys: 'z
want:
|one
error: yes

=== <C-o> and <C-i> go through the jump list
text:
|one
two
three
four
keys: 3GG<C-o><C-o><C-i>
want:
one
two
|three
four

=== a search is a jump
text:
|one
two
three
keys: /three<CR><C-o>
want:
|one
two
three

=== :N is a jump
text:
|one
two
three
keys: :3<CR><C-o>
want:
|one
two
three

=== '[ and '] are the last change's ends
text:
|one
two
three
four
keys: jyjG'[
want:
one
|two
three
four

=== '. is the last change
text:
one
|two
three
keys: xgg`.
want:
one
|wo
three

=== `^ is where the insert mode was left
text:
|one
two
keys: Aab<Esc>j`^
want:
onea|b
two

=== a mark in an Ex range
text:
|a
b
c
d
keys: jmajmb:'a,'bd<CR>
want:
a
|d

=== :delm deletes marks
text:
|one
two
keys: majmb:delm a<CR>'b'a
want:
one
|two
error: yes

=== :mark sets a mark at a line
text:
|one
two
three
keys: :3mark c<CR>'c
want:
one
two
|three

=== a mark in the visual mode moves its end
text:
|one
two
three
keys: Gmaggv'ad
want:
|hree
